# ctx: teardown + build after changes

When you change ctx (Rust, the dashboard in `src/dashboard.html`, config behavior, or hooks), finish with a full local reinstall cycle — do not skip unless the user explicitly says not to.

## 1. Teardown

```bash
which ctx && ctx setup --uninstall || true
pkill -f "ctx proxy" 2>/dev/null || true
pkill -f "ctx dashboard" 2>/dev/null || true
rm -rf ~/.ctx
rm -f ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.ctx.{proxy,dashboard,ingest,experiment-tick}.plist
```

Experiment plan state (`experiment-plan.toml`, journal, tick state) is mirrored to `~/Library/Application Support/ctx/experiment/` on every save. `ctx setup` restores it automatically when `~/.ctx` was wiped.

Clean MCP registrations if uninstall missed them (settings.json, mcp.json).

## 2. Build

The dashboard is a single self-contained file (`src/dashboard.html`, HTML + CSS + JS inline) embedded into the binary via `include_str!`. There is no stitch or build step: edit it directly and reinstall.

```bash
cd ~/Documents/ctx   # or the repo root
source "$HOME/.cargo/env"
cargo install --locked --path .
```

## 3. Setup + verify

```bash
ctx setup --yes
ctx status
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" http://127.0.0.1:8789/
```

Tell the user to **Reload Window** in the IDE after setup.

## Metrics rule

Never show catalog placeholder tool counts (e.g. hardcoded 156) when MCP usage is not indexed. Use `tool_metrics_ready()` / observed history only; show `unknown` or `—` until ingest has MCP data.
